{"assets":["/statement-assets/14790f1c583c7b13efb48408408af947ebdbcec0a18388d514e2c8c01dca05ad.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1286","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. LCC"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"An infinitely long Line Chillland Collider (LCC) was built in Chillland. There are $$$n$$$ pipes with coordinates $$$x_i$$$ that are connected to LCC. When the experiment starts at time 0, $$$i$$$-th proton flies from the $$$i$$$-th pipe with speed $$$v_i$$$. It flies to the right with probability $$$p_i$$$ and flies to the left with probability $$$(1 - p_i)$$$. The "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"duration of the experiment"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is determined as the time of the first collision of any two protons. In case there is no collision, the duration of the experiment is considered to be zero."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find the expected value of the duration of the experiment."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/14790f1c583c7b13efb48408408af947ebdbcec0a18388d514e2c8c01dca05ad.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"Illustration for the first example"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of input contains one integer $$$n$$$ — the number of pipes ($$$1 \\le n \\le 10^5$$$). Each of the following $$$n$$$ lines contains three integers $$$x_i$$$, $$$v_i$$$, $$$p_i$$$ — the coordinate of the $$$i$$$-th pipe, the speed of the $$$i$$$-th proton and the probability that the $$$i$$$-th proton flies to the right in percentage points ($$$-10^9 \\le x_i \\le 10^9, 1 \\le v \\le 10^6, 0 \\le p_i \\le 100$$$). It is guaranteed that all $$$x_i$$$ are distinct and sorted in increasing order."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It's possible to prove that the answer can always be represented as a fraction $$$P/Q$$$, where $$$P$$$ is an integer and $$$Q$$$ is a natural number not divisible by $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$. In this case, print $$$P \\cdot Q^{-1}$$$ modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n1 1 100\n3 1 0\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n7 10 0\n9 4 86\n14 5 100\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n6 4 50\n11 25 50\n13 16 50\n15 8 50\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n150902884\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"1286D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1286/problem/D"}